{
  "topic": "What if the Moon disappeared",
  "language": "en",
  "format": "long",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "What If the Moon Disappeared? 🌙",
  "hook": "What would happen if the Moon vanished forever tonight?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "luna_hook",
      "narration": "What would happen if the Moon vanished forever tonight?",
      "on_screen_text": "What if the Moon vanished?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "vanished?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_vanish",
      "narration": "No explosion, no warning. You look up, and suddenly it's just gone.",
      "on_screen_text": "Suddenly, it's gone",
      "highlight_words": [
        "gone"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "luna_orbit",
      "narration": "It's about two hundred and forty thousand miles away. Does such a distant rock really matter that much?",
      "on_screen_text": "Does a distant rock matter?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "matter?"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "est_hook",
      "narration": "Here's a hint: it would change the night, the sea, the animals and, given enough time, even the climate.",
      "on_screen_text": "Night, sea, animals, climate",
      "highlight_words": [
        "climate"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_switch",
      "narration": "I'm Leo, and today we're switching off the Moon to see what breaks first.",
      "on_screen_text": "Let's switch off the Moon",
      "highlight_words": [
        "off"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_moon",
      "narration": "Let's start with the first night. The full Moon is by far the brightest thing in our night sky.",
      "on_screen_text": "The lamp of the night",
      "highlight_words": [
        "lamp"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The first night"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_fade",
      "narration": "Switch it off, and every night would be as dark as a new moon night.",
      "on_screen_text": "Every night, in the dark",
      "highlight_words": [
        "dark"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_stars",
      "narration": "Far from cities, the sky would fill with stars. Astronomers would be delighted.",
      "on_screen_text": "A sky full of stars",
      "highlight_words": [
        "stars"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_lions",
      "narration": "So would many lions: in places like the Serengeti they eat best on moonless nights, when it's harder to see them coming.",
      "on_screen_text": "Lions hunt better",
      "highlight_words": [
        "better"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_coral_sync",
      "narration": "The sea would be in trouble. Many corals use moonlight as a clock, to release their eggs almost all at once.",
      "on_screen_text": "Corals use the Moon",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Moon"
      ],
      "sfx": "bubbles",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_coral_lost",
      "narration": "Without that signal they'd lose track. It already happens: near artificial lights, they spawn one to three days early.",
      "on_screen_text": "Without it, they lose track",
      "highlight_words": [
        "lose"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ecl_solar",
      "narration": "And goodbye, solar eclipses. Only the Moon can cover the Sun completely in our sky.",
      "on_screen_text": "Goodbye, eclipses",
      "highlight_words": [
        "eclipses"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_tide_pull",
      "narration": "Now let's look at the sea: the Moon pulls harder on Earth's near side than on its far side, and that stretches the oceans.",
      "on_screen_text": "The Moon stretches the oceans",
      "highlight_words": [
        "stretches"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The sea"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_tide_spin",
      "narration": "Earth spins inside those two bulges of water. That's why many coasts get two high tides a day.",
      "on_screen_text": "Two high tides a day",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Two"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_tide_sun",
      "narration": "So would the tides stop? No, the Sun makes them too, with about half the Moon's force.",
      "on_screen_text": "The Sun makes tides too",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Sun"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_tide_none",
      "narration": "Without the Moon, only the Sun's tides would remain: much smaller, and always at the same times of day.",
      "on_screen_text": "Small tides only",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Small"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_beach",
      "narration": "Today, the strip of shore the sea covers and uncovers is full of life: crabs, mussels and birds looking for food.",
      "on_screen_text": "A strip full of life",
      "highlight_words": [
        "life"
      ],
      "sfx": "bubbles",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_small",
      "narration": "With such small tides, that home would shrink dramatically.",
      "on_screen_text": "That home would shrink",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shrink"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ecl_size",
      "narration": "Mini challenge: the Sun is four hundred times wider than the Moon. So why does the Moon win at tides?",
      "on_screen_text": "Why does the Moon win?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "win?"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_tide_why",
      "narration": "Because it's far, far closer, and tidal force fades very quickly with distance.",
      "on_screen_text": "Because it's closer!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "closer!"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "est_tilt",
      "narration": "The biggest change would also be the slowest. Earth spins tilted by about twenty-three degrees.",
      "on_screen_text": "A tilted planet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "tilted"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Earth's axis"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "est_june",
      "narration": "That tilt creates the seasons: when the north leans toward the Sun, it's summer there.",
      "on_screen_text": "The tilt makes seasons",
      "highlight_words": [
        "seasons"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "est_december",
      "narration": "Half a year later, it's the south's turn.",
      "on_screen_text": "Then it's the south's turn",
      "highlight_words": [
        "south's"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "lun_tilt",
      "narration": "The Moon helps keep that axis quite steady. It shifts only a couple of degrees over tens of thousands of years.",
      "on_screen_text": "The Moon steadies the axis",
      "highlight_words": [
        "steadies"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_mars",
      "narration": "Look at Mars, which has no large moon. Over millions of years, its tilt may have swung between zero and sixty degrees.",
      "on_screen_text": "Mars wobbles",
      "highlight_words": [
        "wobbles"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_wobble",
      "narration": "Without the Moon, Earth's axis could vary a lot too. In the nineties, one calculation allowed up to eighty-five degrees.",
      "on_screen_text": "And Earth?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Earth?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_hot",
      "narration": "With the axis lying that flat, one pole would get sunlight for months while the other stayed dark. The seasons would be brutal.",
      "on_screen_text": "Brutal seasons",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Brutal"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_debate",
      "narration": "But science corrects itself. Newer studies point to much slower changes, which wouldn't rule out life on their own.",
      "on_screen_text": "Science corrects itself",
      "highlight_words": [
        "corrects"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s29",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_bary",
      "narration": "Would Earth fly off into space? No, it would keep circling the Sun; it would only lose a small wobble.",
      "on_screen_text": "Earth stays on course",
      "highlight_words": [
        "stays"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Myths and surprises"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_shield",
      "narration": "Would we lose our shield? Not really: the Moon is too small a target to stop most asteroids.",
      "on_screen_text": "It's not a shield",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shield"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s31",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "lun_impact",
      "narration": "The amazing part is the past. The leading idea is that the Moon was born in a giant impact, about four and a half billion years ago.",
      "on_screen_text": "Born in a giant impact",
      "highlight_words": [
        "impact"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s32",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "lun_close",
      "narration": "At first it was much, much closer, and it would have looked enormous in the sky.",
      "on_screen_text": "It once looked enormous",
      "highlight_words": [
        "enormous"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_day",
      "narration": "Ever since, the tides have been slowing our spin. One point four billion years ago, a day lasted just over eighteen hours.",
      "on_screen_text": "18-hour days",
      "highlight_words": [
        "18-hour"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s34",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ecl_future",
      "narration": "And today the Moon drifts away about an inch and a half per year. We measure it with lasers, thanks to mirrors left by the Apollo program.",
      "on_screen_text": "Drifting 1.5 inches a year",
      "highlight_words": [
        "1.5"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "luna_full",
      "narration": "So don't worry: it's leaving, but about as fast as your fingernails grow.",
      "on_screen_text": "Leaving very slowly",
      "highlight_words": [
        "slowly"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s36",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sl_moon",
      "narration": "Tonight, look at it differently: it moves the sea, guides the corals and helps keep our planet steady.",
      "on_screen_text": "Look at it differently",
      "highlight_words": [
        "differently"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s37",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "lun_outro",
      "narration": "What should we switch off next? Tell me in the comments.",
      "on_screen_text": "What do we switch off next?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "next?"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ],
